Abstraction:

--> Hiding Implementation details and show only the required functionality to user.

User Know --> What to do
User dont want to know --> How internally it works

1. Abstract class --> Partial abstraction
2. Interface --> Full abstraction/contract


Abstract class:
1. cannot instantiated.
2. acts as blueprint of child class
3. contains:
    1. Abstract method ---> has declaration only and it doesnot have implementation : eg. abstract void start() -->Child class MUST implement it;
    2. Normal method --> has declaration  and  implementation
    3. variables
    4. constructor
4. Class should have 'abstract' keyword

features of Abstract class:
features                Supported
1.Object creation           NO
2.Constructor               YES
3.variable                  YES
4.Normal Methods            YES
5.Abstract method           YES
6.Code Resue                YES

